 D['primer']=[dict(term=t,meaning=m) for t,m in [
 ('Host / endpoint','A computer or device on which programs run, such as a laptop or server.'),
 ('Server / client','A server provides a service; a client requests it. One device can perform both roles.'),
 ('Operating system / application','The OS manages the device’s resources. An application performs a task using those resources.'),
 ('Network / protocol','A network connects devices. A protocol gives rules for their communication.'),
 ('Packet / header / payload','A packet carries data. Its header carries control information; its payload is the carried content, which can itself contain another layer’s header.'),
 ('Address / port','An IP address identifies a network endpoint; a port helps identify a transport service or conversation.'),
 ('Vulnerability / exploit / payload','A vulnerability is a weakness. An exploit takes advantage of it. A payload is the action or code delivered or run.'),
 ('Authentication / authorization','Authentication checks a claimed identity. Authorization decides what that identity may do.'),
 ('Firewall / detection','A firewall enforces communication rules. Detection identifies suspicious activity; an alert needs investigation.'),
 ('Key / hash / signature','A key controls a cryptographic operation. A hash is a digest for comparison. A signature provides verifiable authorization or origin under a trusted key.'),
 ('Public / private key','A public key may be distributed. Its corresponding private key must stay secret. Which person’s key you use depends on the goal.'),
 ('Business impact','Explain what information, money, service, or trust is at risk, and why your proposed defense addresses it.')]]
 D['primer'] += [dict(term=t,meaning=m) for t,m in [('Transaction / ledger','A transaction records a transfer or other event. A ledger is the record of those events.'),('Block / blockchain','A block groups records and control information. A blockchain links blocks using cryptographic commitments to earlier history.'),('Consensus / validation','Validation checks the rules. Consensus is how participants agree on an accepted history despite competing or faulty participants.'),('Distributed / decentralized','Distributed work or storage is spread across systems. Decentralized authority is spread across decision makers. A distributed system can still be centrally controlled.')]]
